cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Loom — the feature-completeness skill of the Forge suite"
message: "If you use Loom, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mohammed
    family-names: Nasher
    alias: mhd-nasher
repository-code: "https://github.com/mhd-nasher/loom"
url: "https://github.com/mhd-nasher"
abstract: >
  Loom is a self-contained, stack-aware feature-completeness engine for AI coding assistants. It
  takes one vague feature ask and returns the whole fabric — every actor, user flow, state, edge
  case, data-lifecycle moment, and Given/When/Then acceptance criterion — and it audits
  already-built features for the forgotten details that burn in production. Every dimension the
  stack profile applies is either specified or explicitly cut with a stated reason (the One-Weave
  Law): one feature per run, discoveries outside the goal are parked and routed to their owning
  sibling — with a strict-return subagent handoff — and the moment the weave is complete Loom
  declares done and stops. Findings carry stable F-### IDs. Firebase/Flutter/Next/Stripe is the
  flagship profile; websites, mobile apps, and APIs/backend systems are all covered. Part of the
  Forge suite: it routes structure to Cairn, tests to Anvil, quality to Lens, security severity
  to Bastion, and rollout mechanics to Relay.
keywords:
